"I'd like to apply for the Data Scientist role in London.",

"I'm finishing an MSc in Health Data Science at UCL and I currently work as a data analyst at TikTok Shop UK, mostly on merchant growth. Why a cohort converts. Which lever actually moved a number, and which one only looked like it did. Before that I built LLM evaluation systems for a pharmaceutical client. Both jobs came down to the same problem: deciding what to measure before anyone had decided what to measure.",

"That is what caught my attention about this role. You are not hiring someone to maintain an analytics function, you are hiring someone to build one. Sixty million projects in under two years means the interesting questions are behavioural now, and the metric definitions set this year are the ones everything downstream inherits. I would rather be in the room for those decisions than unpick them in three years.",

