"On experiments: at DS Digital Technology I designed blinded paired A/B tests to find out whether a medically reviewed knowledge graph genuinely improved answer quality, and owned it end to end, from hypothesis to recommendation. I also ran a repeated-measures study across 12 audience segments and 15 marketing touchpoints. I used Friedman and permutation tests rather than the parametric defaults because the data would not support them, and a confident wrong answer would have been worse than a cautious one. The client shipped per-segment playbooks off the back of it.",

